{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Health and environment] 2026 Ebola epidemic — The United Nations reports that daily Ebola cases in the Democratic Republic of the Congo declined from about 120 to 80, while 10 of 62 affected health zones record no new infections for more than 22 days."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] 2024 Bangladesh quota reform movement, Controversies related to Sheikh Hasina, death — A court in Bangladesh sentences seven Awami League leaders who were former officials in former prime minister Sheikh Hasina's government to death in absentia over their role in deadly crackdowns on the anti-government protests in 2024."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Femicide in Latin America, Gender inequality in El Salvador — A court in El Salvador sentences a man to death for stalking and aggravated femicide, the first death sentence for this crime in the country's history."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Phillips family disappearances — A New Zealand inquiry finds that police and Oranga Tamariki failed to act on warnings that Tom Phillips might abduct his three children and possessed firearms, contributing to missed opportunities to prevent or end their nearly four-year di"}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] The Brazilian public prosecutor's office files a civil action against Vale, the world's largest iron ore producer and one of Brazil's biggest companies, as well as the national mining agency and the Minas Gerais state government. The lawsui"}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Former Golden Dawn spokesperson Ilias Kasidiaris is released from prison in Domokos, Phthiotis, Greece, after serving part of a 13-year sentence for leading a criminal organization and announces plans to return to politics, although he rema"}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] ProRail services across northern and central parts of the Netherlands are disrupted by a sabotage operation after pipes are attached to tracks, resulting in the failure of railway signals."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Romanian farmers clash with gendarmes in Bucharest during protests against live export restrictions and other policies. The confrontations leave 24 people injured, including eight gendarmes, while police detain 26 protesters."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Politics and elections] Reactions to the 2026 Iran war — United States representative Thomas Massie files articles for impeachment against defense secretary Pete Hegseth for allegedly violating the War Powers Resolution by declaring war against Iran without congressional approval."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Sports] 2026 Asian Games — The Italian cruise ship Costa Serena docks in Nagoya, Japan, to house about 4,000 Asian Games athletes and officials as delegations report accommodation problems, including undersized beds, leaking sinks, and room shortages."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Sports] In association football, UEFA announces that the Champions League finals in 2028 and 2029 will be held at the Allianz Arena in Munich, Germany, and Camp Nou in Barcelona, Spain, respectively."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 34315, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Sports] The World Athletics Championships in 2029 and 2031 are awarded to Nairobi, Kenya, and Munich, Germany, respectively. It will be the first event to be held on the continent of Africa."}
